<main id="content"><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Umicom Framework &amp; Applications</p><h1>Documents, drafts and memory</h1><p class="lead">Follow a Notes working copy through shared Framework services.</p></header>
<h2>One file, several useful representations</h2><p>A tab is the visible place where a document is shown. A working copy is the draft being edited. The saved file is the version on disk. These representations can differ while you type. Saving, closing and switching tabs must therefore use the document service rather than treating whatever text is visible as the only state.</p><p>Framework's coordinator connects the store, view model, history and provider. The view snapshot contains a small preview; complete-text APIs return the rest of a larger draft. A component that copies only the preview must not write it back as though it were the full file.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Source location</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Coordinator public interface</td><td><a href="https://github.com/umicom-foundation/umicom-framework/blob/main/include/umicom/document/coordinator.h"><code>include/umicom/document/coordinator.h</code></a></td></tr><tr><td>View and complete-text interface</td><td><a href="https://github.com/umicom-foundation/umicom-framework/blob/main/include/umicom/ui/document_view.h"><code>include/umicom/ui/document_view.h</code></a></td></tr><tr><td>Coordinator implementation</td><td><a href="https://github.com/umicom-foundation/umicom-framework/blob/main/src/document/coordinator.c"><code>src/document/coordinator.c</code></a></td></tr><tr><td>View implementation</td><td><a href="https://github.com/umicom-foundation/umicom-framework/blob/main/src/ui/document_view.c"><code>src/ui/document_view.c</code></a></td></tr><tr><td>Document regression checks</td><td><a href="https://github.com/umicom-foundation/umicom-framework/blob/main/tests/document/test_source_files.c"><code>tests/document/test_source_files.c</code></a></td></tr><tr><td>Complete application example</td><td><a href="https://github.com/umicom-foundation/umicom-framework/blob/main/examples/editor_workflow/complete_document.c"><code>examples/editor_workflow/complete_document.c</code></a></td></tr><tr><td>Example CMake target</td><td><a href="https://github.com/umicom-foundation/umicom-framework/blob/main/examples/editor_workflow/CMakeLists.txt"><code>examples/editor_workflow/CMakeLists.txt</code></a></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Read a complete example</h2><p>The program below creates an in-memory Notes source document, changes text beyond the small preview and restores it with Undo. It does not save a real file. That makes it a useful first exercise before adding filesystem operations.</p><details><summary>Show the complete source</summary><pre><code>@UMICOM_SITE_DOCUMENT_EXAMPLE@</code></pre></details><h2>Memory ownership</h2><p>Read each copy operation together with its release function. A copied string has a lifetime independent of the widget that displays it. Free it with the API named by its contract; do not guess that every pointer should use the same allocator. Keep the store, coordinator and view model alive for the operations that borrow them, then destroy them in their required order.</p><h2>Compile and run</h2><p>Use the SDK prefix you installed following the <a href="../build-and-publish.html">build guide</a>. Configure the existing example directory, then build the <code>umicom-notes-document</code> target:</p><h3>Windows</h3><pre><code>Set-Location "C:\umicom\Umicom-Applications"
$env:Path = "C:\msys64\ucrt64\bin;$env:Path"
cmake -S framework/examples/editor_workflow -B build/notes-document -G Ninja -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="C:/umicom/installed/development" -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER="C:/msys64/ucrt64/bin/gcc.exe" -DCMAKE_MAKE_PROGRAM="C:/msys64/ucrt64/bin/ninja.exe"
cmake --build build/notes-document --target umicom-notes-document
ctest --test-dir build/notes-document --no-tests=error --output-on-failure -R '^notes\.document\.complete$'</code></pre><h3>Linux</h3><pre><code>cd "$HOME/umicom/Umicom-Applications"
cmake -S framework/examples/editor_workflow -B build/notes-document -G Ninja -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$HOME/umicom/installed/development"
cmake --build build/notes-document --target umicom-notes-document
ctest --test-dir build/notes-document --no-tests=error --output-on-failure -R '^notes\.document\.complete$'</code></pre><p>This executable links <code>Umicom::document</code>. The unchanged smaller search example lives beside it. A missing SDK is a configuration problem, not a reason to copy private Framework source files into the project.</p><h2>Save and close by identity</h2><p>Selection can change while a dialog is open. Capture the document identity when beginning Save As or confirming a close. Do not later substitute whichever tab happens to be active. A file modified by another application also needs conflict handling; a different spelling of its path must not bypass the check.</p><h2>Bounded editing</h2><p>The current complete-draft path supports up to 8 MiB of decoded UTF-8 text per document. Undo history and dynamically allocated draft storage also have budgets. A size rejection must leave the original work usable. These limits do not bound every GTK or application allocation and are not a streaming large-file design.</p><h2>Practise</h2><p>Change the variable name being replaced and update the expected result in a practice copy. Run the test again. Next, shorten the document and verify that Undo restores the full earlier text. Explain which function owns each allocation before introducing file saving or another thread.</p>
</main><footer><strong>Umicom Foundation</strong><p>Learn from the source. Build with shared components.</p><a href="../contributing.html">Improve these guides</a> · <a href="https://github.com/umicom-foundation">GitHub organisation</a></footer></body></html>
